
[TestRateVMShortWindow/-search.maxStalenessInterval_limits_how_far_back_the_sample_before_the_window_is_used - 1]
- description: -search.maxStalenessInterval limits how far back the sample before the window is used
  content: |
    - record: foo:rate
      expr: rate(foo[15m])
  output: |
    2 |   expr: rate(foo[15m])
                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
                `rate()` needs a window of at least 18m with the `10m` scrape_interval of `prom`
                VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com: vmalert evaluates the rule with
                instant queries with a 5m step, the query step, default vmalert -datasource.queryStep (5m),
                limited by -search.maxStalenessInterval=2m on `prom`, and VictoriaMetrics uses the last
                sample before the window only if it's at most 2m before the window. A `[15m]` window can
                have a single sample, so it can return no results or wrong ones.
  problem:
    reporter: promql/rate
    summary: duration too small
    details: 'vmalert evaluates rules with instant queries and sends `-datasource.queryStep` as the step, 5m by default, or `step` from the group `params`. VictoriaMetrics only uses the last sample before the window if it''s at most one step before the window. With a scrape interval longer than the step a window shorter than two scrape intervals minus the step can have a single sample: `rate()` and `irate()` return nothing and `increase()` returns 0. `deriv()` only uses samples inside the window and always needs two scrape intervals.'
    diagnostics:
        - message: '`rate()` needs a window of at least 18m with the `10m` scrape_interval of `prom` VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com: vmalert evaluates the rule with instant queries with a 5m step, the query step, default vmalert -datasource.queryStep (5m), limited by -search.maxStalenessInterval=2m on `prom`, and VictoriaMetrics uses the last sample before the window only if it''s at most 2m before the window. A `[15m]` window can have a single sample, so it can return no results or wrong ones.'
          firstcolumn: 1
          lastcolumn: 14
          kind: 0
    lines:
        first: 2
        last: 2
    severity: 1
    anchor: 0

