[TestRateVMShortWindow/deriv_needs_2x_scrape_interval_whatever_the_step - 1]
- description: deriv needs 2x scrape interval whatever the step
  content: |
    - name: g
      params:
        step: ["15m"]
      rules:
      - record: foo:deriv
        expr: deriv(foo[15m])
  output: |
    6 |     expr: deriv(foo[15m])
                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
                  `deriv()` needs a window of at least 20m with the `10m` scrape_interval of `prom`
                  VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com: `deriv()` only uses samples inside
                  the window, so it needs two scrape intervals. A `[15m]` window can have a single sample,
                  so it can return no results or wrong ones.
