                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
                `rollup_rate()` needs a window of at least 1m with the `1m` scrape_interval of `prom`
                VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com: VictoriaMetrics uses the sample before
                the window only if it's at most 5m before the window. A `[30s]` window can miss the samples
                `rollup_rate()` needs, so it can return `0` or nothing instead of the real value.
  problem:
    reporter: promql/rate
    summary: duration too small
    details: '`rollup_rate()`, `rollup_deriv()`, `rollup_increase()` and `rollup_delta()` calculate changes between adjacent samples. When the window has a single sample, VictoriaMetrics pairs it with the sample before the window only if that one is at most 5m before the window, or `-search.minStalenessInterval` when it''s longer. Otherwise these functions return `0` instead of the real change, so the window must be at least two scrape intervals minus that limit, and at least one scrape interval.'
    diagnostics:
        - message: '`rollup_rate()` needs a window of at least 1m with the `1m` scrape_interval of `prom` VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com: VictoriaMetrics uses the sample before the window only if it''s at most 5m before the window. A `[30s]` window can miss the samples `rollup_rate()` needs, so it can return `0` or nothing instead of the real value.'
